1
00:05:21,428 --> 00:05:27,428
Only monsters play God.

2
00:10:42,857 --> 00:10:48,857
Frankenstein is a drama, fantasy, horror film directed by Guillermo del Toro.

3
00:16:04,285 --> 00:16:10,285
Victor Frankenstein, a brilliant but egotistical scientist, brings a creature to life in a monstrous
experiment that ultimately leads to the undoing of both the creator and his tragic creation.

4
00:21:25,714 --> 00:21:31,714
Victor Frankenstein, played by Oscar Isaac.

5
00:26:47,142 --> 00:26:53,142
The Creature, played by Jacob Elordi.

6
00:32:08,571 --> 00:32:14,571
Harlander, played by Christoph Waltz.

7
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:36,000
Elizabeth / Claire Frankenstein, played by Mia Goth.

8
00:42:51,428 --> 00:42:57,428
William Frankenstein, played by Felix Kammerer.

9
00:48:12,857 --> 00:48:18,857
Leopold Frankenstein, played by Charles Dance.

10
00:53:34,285 --> 00:53:40,285
Frankenstein is a 2025 American Gothic science fiction drama film produced, written, and
directed by Guillermo del Toro, based on the 1818 novel by Mary Shelley.

11
00:58:55,714 --> 00:59:01,714
The film stars Oscar Isaac as Victor Frankenstein and Jacob Elordi as the
Creature, with Mia Goth and Christoph Waltz in supporting roles.

12
01:04:17,142 --> 01:04:23,142
The story follows the life of Frankenstein, an egotistical scientist whose
experiment in creating new life results in dangerous consequences.

13
01:09:38,571 --> 01:09:44,571
Del Toro had long imagined a faithful Frankenstein film as a "dream project".

14
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
This was initially in development for Universal Pictures, with del Toro casting frequent collaborator
Doug Jones as the Creature, and Bernie Wrightson being considered for the monster's design.

15
01:20:21,428 --> 01:20:27,428
However, Universal suspended the project in relation to
its planned Dark Universe franchise.

16
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
Netflix revived the project in 2023, with Elordi
instead portraying the Creature.

17
01:31:04,285 --> 01:31:10,285
Filming took place from February to September 2024.

18
01:36:25,714 --> 01:36:31,714
Wrightson had died in 2017, and the illustrated compilation Bernie
Wrightson's Frankenstein was a key inspiration for the film's look.

19
01:41:47,142 --> 01:41:53,142
Frankenstein premiered at the 82nd Venice
International Film Festival on August 30, 2025.

20
01:47:08,571 --> 01:47:14,571
The film was released on Netflix.

21
01:52:30,000 --> 01:52:36,000
It had a limited theatrical release in the United States from October
17 and was globally released on November 7 on Netflix.

22
01:57:51,428 --> 01:57:57,428
The film received generally positive reviews from critics.

23
02:03:12,857 --> 02:03:18,857
Both the National Board of Review and the American Film
Institute named it as one of the top ten films of 2025.

24
02:08:34,285 --> 02:08:40,285
It received five nominations at the 83rd Golden Globe
Awards, including Best Motion Picture – Drama.

25
02:13:55,714 --> 02:14:01,714
It received nine nominations at the 98th Academy Awards, including Best
Picture, Best Adapted Screenplay and Best Supporting Actor (Elordi).

26
02:19:17,142 --> 02:19:23,142
The film explores themes of monster, based on novel or
book, supernatural, surgeon, mad scientist.

27
02:24:38,571 --> 02:24:44,571
The tone is dark and emotional.
